{"id": "EUVD-2026-60090", "enisaUuid": "925a7613-2cc5-3553-9fe5-a755745e0ed1", "description": "openssl_encrypt versions before 1.4.6 contain a key derivation flaw in sequential XOR composition mode where the last stage cancels out during key generation. When configured with a single KDF and no prior hashing stage, attackers can bypass memory-hard key derivation and perform offline password cracking at SHA-256 speed instead of the configured KDF cost.", "datePublished": "2026-08-17T11:04:40", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-01T15:20:48", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/jahlives/openssl_encrypt/security/advisories/GHSA-vxf9-vwp6-2w43", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/openssl-encrypt-before-kdf-bypass-via-sequential-xor"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74871", "PYSEC-2026-3976", "GHSA-pj8r-rv9w-cfg8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.11, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "51f9f724-be23-3dae-9b3a-118c10e8966b", "product": {"name": "openssl_encrypt", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.4.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "318bff22-8834-318a-b7f0-fc9081ce81f1", "vendor": {"name": "jahlives"}}], "isExploited": false}